          "why": "The velocity is momentarily zero at the turning point, but gravity continues to accelerate the ball downward.",
          "sol": "Step 1: At the highest point, the ball momentarily stops moving upward.\nStep 2: Its instantaneous velocity is 0 m/s.\nStep 3: Gravity still acts downward, so acceleration is −g.",
          "hint": "Separate the momentary velocity from the continuing effect of gravity.",
