          "why": "Halving the area doubles pressure when force remains constant.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Let the area of Y be A.\nStep 2: The area of X is A/2.\nStep 3: Pressure on X is F/(A/2) = 2F/A.",
          "hint": "Pressure is inversely proportional to area when force is constant.",
