          "why": "Density differences in a gravitational field drive the circulation.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The water warms and expands.\nStep 2: Its density decreases relative to the cooler water.\nStep 3: The warmer, less dense water rises under gravity.",
          "hint": "Consider how heating affects volume and density.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "topic": "Heat Transfer by Convection",
          "conceptId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_heat_transfer_by_convection",
