          "why": "50,000 ÷ 0.25 = 200,000 J/kg.",
          "sol": "Step 1: L = 50,000/0.25.\nStep 2: L = 200,000 J/kg.",
          "hint": "Rearrange Q = mL to make L the subject.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "topic": "Specific Latent Heat",
          "conceptId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_specific_latent_heat",
