          "why": "At constant power, plateau duration reflects the energy needed for the phase change.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Energy supplied equals power multiplied by time.\nStep 2: A longer plateau at the same power means more energy is supplied during the phase change.\nStep 3: This can indicate a larger sample mass or a larger total latent-energy requirement.",
          "hint": "At a constant input rate, a longer time means more energy supplied.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "topic": "Heating Curves",
          "conceptId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_heating_curves",
          "skillId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics",
