          "why": "Energy leaves the substance as latent heat during the phase change.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The substance reaches its freezing point.\nStep 2: It releases latent heat as liquid becomes solid.\nStep 3: Its temperature stays constant until freezing is complete under the stated conditions.",
          "hint": "Consider the energy released during freezing.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "topic": "Cooling Curves",
          "conceptId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_cooling_curves",
          "skillId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "subskillId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_q2"
