          "why": "Air movement often reduces the build-up of vapour immediately above the liquid.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Evaporated water vapour accumulates near a still surface.\nStep 2: Moving air carries some vapour away.\nStep 3: Evaporation can continue more rapidly.",
          "hint": "Think about what happens to water vapour near the surface.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "topic": "Factors Affecting Evaporation",
          "conceptId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_factors_affecting_evaporation",
          "skillId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics",
          "subskillId": "physics_temperature_and_thermal_physics_q3"
