          "why": "When the surrounding air is humid, it generally accepts additional water vapour less readily.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Humid air already contains a high amount of water vapour relative to its capacity.\nStep 2: The difference that drives evaporation is smaller.\nStep 3: Water generally evaporates more slowly.",
