          "why": "Rolling resistance is generally lower than sliding friction in this application.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Identify the relative motion of the parts.\nStep 2: Ball bearings allow rolling.\nStep 3: Relate rolling to resistance.",
          "hint": "They change the type of motion between surfaces.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "force_motion_and_mechanics",
          "topic": "Reducing and Increasing Friction",
          "conceptId": "physics_force_motion_and_mechanics_reducing_and_increasing_friction",
