          "why": "A pressure difference is needed to move the liquid upwards.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Air enters through the hole.\nStep 2: The pressure inside the straw may no longer fall sufficiently.\nStep 3: The pressure difference becomes too small to raise liquid effectively.",
          "hint": "Air can enter through the hole.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "pressure",
          "topic": "The Drinking Straw",
          "conceptId": "physics_pressure_the_drinking_straw",
