          "why": "This prevents the object's weight from producing a toppling moment about the edge.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Identify the object's supporting base.\nStep 2: Check where the vertical line through the centre of gravity meets the ground.\nStep 3: For stability, it should fall within the base.",
          "hint": "Consider the base of support.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "moments_and_equilibrium",
          "topic": "The Line of Action of Weight",
