          "why": "The potential difference is the kinetic energy gained divided by the magnitude of the electron charge.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Write KE = eV.\nStep 2: Rearrange to V = KE/e.\nStep 3: Substitute V = (3.2 × 10⁻¹⁷)/(1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹).\nStep 4: Calculate the ratio.",
          "hint": "Rearrange KE = eV to make V the subject.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "cathode_rays",
          "topic": "Acceleration of Electrons by Potential Difference",
          "conceptId": "physics_cathode_rays_acceleration_of_electrons_by_potential_difference",
