          "why": "Equal-amplitude waves in opposite phase have equal and opposite displacements, so they cancel at points of complete destructive interference.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Identify key concept: Define the required principles for Destructive Interference.\nStep 2: Apply governing rule: Equal-amplitude waves in opposite phase have equal and opposite displacements, so they cancel at points of complete destructive interference.\nStep 3: State the final conclusion: When they arrive in opposite phase",
          "hint": "A crest of one must align with a trough of the other.",
