          "why": "The material in which light travels more slowly has the higher absolute refractive index.",
          "sol": "Step 1: n = c/v.\nStep 2: The vacuum speed c is constant.\nStep 3: A smaller medium speed v gives a larger refractive index.",
          "hint": "The refractive index is inversely related to speed in the medium.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "waves",
          "topic": "Refractive Index",
          "conceptId": "physics_waves_refractive_index",
          "skillId": "physics_waves",
          "subskillId": "physics_waves_q3"
