          "why": "Using Snell's law gives a refractive index of approximately 1.46.",
          "sol": "Step 1: n_glass = n_air sin i / sin r\nStep 2: n_glass = sin 30° / sin 20°\nStep 3: n_glass ≈ 0.500 / 0.342\nStep 4: n_glass ≈ 1.46",
          "hint": "Rearrange Snell's law to n_glass = n_air sin i / sin r.",
          "subject": "physics",
