          "why": "Diffraction depends on wavelength relative to the size of the opening or obstacle.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Sound generally has much longer wavelengths than visible light.\nStep 2: Visible-light wavelengths are extremely small compared with everyday obstacles.\nStep 3: Sound therefore often diffracts more noticeably around such objects.",
          "hint": "Compare the wavelengths of sound and visible light with object sizes.",
