          "why": "A node always has zero resultant displacement.",
          "sol": "Step 1: At a node, the two wave displacements are equal and opposite.\nStep 2: Their resultant displacement is zero.\nStep 3: This remains true throughout the oscillation.",
          "hint": "A node is the point where cancellation is complete.",
          "subject": "physics",
          "chapter": "waves",
          "topic": "Nodes in Stationary Waves",
          "conceptId": "physics_waves_nodes_in_stationary_waves",
