          "why": "Velocity is a vector quantity, so a change in direction is a change in velocity.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The stone's speed remains constant.\nStep 2: Its direction changes as it moves around the circle.\nStep 3: Therefore, its velocity changes.",
          "hint": "Velocity includes both speed and direction.",
          "subject": "physics",
