          "why": "A force perpendicular to displacement does zero work.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The support force acts vertically upward.\nStep 2: The displacement is horizontal.\nStep 3: The force is perpendicular to the displacement, so its work is zero.",
          "hint": "Compare the direction of the force with the direction of displacement.",
          "subject": "physics",
